WEBVTT

00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:04.480
Getting such country-side girls
 on prime time already...

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:07.450
That's the Marketing Section's job.

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:09.980
It's time to move on from rock bands.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:14.040
Amazing. You must get
 a head start in business, huh?

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:18.370
"Choose the hardest job first."
 A rule of the previous boss.

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:21.870
There's something
 I want you to promote.

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:26.870
Let me tell you, it's a job
 straight from Advisor Satomi.

00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:28.750
Satomi...

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:31.510
Who's worked here
 since before the war?

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:37.620
Master Ultima is a genius scientist
 born from an alien and a human.

00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:40.700
A superhuman who travels
 the solar system by rocket.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:44.080
The space beasts he caught in Mars

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:48.450
came to be stationed across the world
 as US Army weapons.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.370
Some say beasts
 went from human enemies

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:53.700
to protectors of peace.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:13.370
Concrete Revolutio
 ~Superhuman Phantasmagoria~

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:20.450
I heard it
 A voice cursing fate

00:01:21.290 --> 00:01:24.660
I found it
 A way to use my power

00:01:24.910 --> 00:01:28.200
What you want are not words,
 are they?

00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:31.870
That love inside
 I want to send it on

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:34.650
Justice is not on my side

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:39.620
The only thing absolute for me
 is myself

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.410
Come on Wakers. Ready, go!

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:46.620
Protecting the illusions
 that somebody dreamed of

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:50.870
will liberate the stagnant sky

00:01:51.580 --> 00:01:56.700
We hurl our unanswerable cries
 at each other

00:01:57.050 --> 00:02:01.660
And they become the reason we live

00:02:02.290 --> 00:02:07.330
What can I do in this
 hopeless world we live in?

00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:11.870
Only those that keep searching

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:15.160
can become the future

00:02:15.290 --> 00:02:19.120
Start the revolution!

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:28.000
(July, the 42nd of Shinka era,
 Offshore of Kikai island, Kyushu region)

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:33.620
No matter how many times I dive,
 nothing.

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:37.510
But the coordinates released by
 the US Army are here.

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:43.540
The large creature to be stationed
 at a US Army base died,

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:47.000
and was dumped
 in the ocean by Kikai island.

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:52.450
"Broken Lance" is what they call
 these kinds of cases.

00:02:52.830 --> 00:02:56.950
Beasts became uncontrollable
 and disposed in Greenland and Spain.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:58.750
Meaning, they were killed.

00:02:58.790 --> 00:03:00.200
But there's nothing.

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:02.450
Maybe it got eaten by fish.

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:04.700
Oh, I didn't eat it.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:08.290
Or... It never existed to begin with.

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:14.250
Where is it really,
 after the fake disposal?

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:18.880
In Tokyo soon.
 We'll have you play out its debut.

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:23.750
The media will be magazines, TV,
 radio, and student word of mouth.

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:25.910
You won't ask why?

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:29.330
If I did,
 I couldn't work at a publicity firm.

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:31.140
But I have an idea.

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:33.900
Oh, I'd like to hear it.

00:03:34.410 --> 00:03:36.620
The return of Okinawa in 3 years...

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:39.900
Dealing with the Japanese's
 beast hatred by then.

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:44.030
Meaning the government.
 It's a Roppongi-related job.

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:47.290
Do you know the Superhuman Bureau?

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:50.790
Tell me, Advisor Satomi.

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:52.910
Remember it.

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:55.370
It's the name of our enemy.

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:01.750
Enemy...

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:03.950
Like I said...

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:07.910
I think you should
 listen a little more closely.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:09.930
To the beasts?

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:13.910
They've been on this planet
 since we were monkeys.

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:17.820
And you're using them for war,
 let alone killing them.

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:20.040
Those superhuman guys...

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:21.330
About that...

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:25.000
After Beastly Radio Wave Japan Inc.
 was destroyed,

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:27.040
less beasts appeared.

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:32.750
We were chasing President Matsumoto,
 Hiroyuki, and GaGon, who ran away.

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:37.870
You still can't remember
 what happened?

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:39.250
Kikko.

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:41.200
You called me that again.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:46.870
Do you think
 I ate the beast or something?

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:49.910
It's like I'm a beast too.

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:54.500
Senpai, it seems like you
 really hate beasts.

00:04:54.700 --> 00:04:56.290
Why is that?

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:00.830
Jiro, the professor is worried.

00:05:00.950 --> 00:05:02.500
Let's go together.

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:08.080
Please lock up.
 Oh, and throw those away too.

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:09.910
Oh, yes.

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:16.580
Hoshinoko, you'll still stay here?
 Your purpose is...

00:05:16.660 --> 00:05:19.450
Hey Ullr, what are beasts?

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:23.000
During this time,
 there was much debate

00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:27.330
about if beasts were evil that should
 be killed or victims of humanity.

00:05:27.790 --> 00:05:31.000
The youth were
 sympathetic towards beasts,

00:05:31.290 --> 00:05:34.040
as if someone was
 making them feel that way.

00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:38.410
To me, they're like elephants
 or lions, but bigger.

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:43.160
But humans tend to interpret beasts
 in a difficult manner.

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:45.500
Probably because among the beasts...

00:05:46.790 --> 00:05:48.910
They're not clippings.

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:51.330
I feel a power from this.

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:55.620
The power of what
 humans call monsters.

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:02.670
Today's peace march will depart
 this school at evening,

00:06:02.950 --> 00:06:06.660
and cover the National Diet Building,
 Ichigaya, and US Embassy.

00:06:06.790 --> 00:06:08.300
It will be extensive.

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:17.940
Will Matsumoto and the others
 come with all these people?

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:21.870
Well, they'd stand out
 if they're with GaGon...

00:06:22.870 --> 00:06:24.200
Excuse me.

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:29.750
I heard there's something special at
 today's protest, but do you know?

00:06:30.250 --> 00:06:32.750
You're not from this school. Well...

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:34.330
Where are you from?

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:35.790
Your affiliation?

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:38.080
Affiliation? You mean our sect?

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:41.580
No, we're looking for
 Mr. Shoji Matsumoto.

00:06:41.870 --> 00:06:43.460
Where'd you hear that name?

00:06:44.450 --> 00:06:45.380
So he's here!

00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:46.510
Idiot.

00:06:47.370 --> 00:06:50.510
I showed a pic to a refrigerator
 truck dealer in Kagoshima.

00:06:51.290 --> 00:06:54.510
It was Matsumoto who
 hauled and transported something.

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:57.830
That's the beast
 the US Army supposedly disposed.

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:00.580
But can Matsumoto negotiate with them?

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:04.520
Anyway, the refrigerator truck
 disappeared around here.

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:09.400
I guess Ogre Emi couldn't
 be a student after all.

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:12.250
We have to try again. Let's go.

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:18.660
You guys are beasts yourselves.

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:27.510
Jiro.
 Hey, kid!

00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:31.010
You gave me this to make beasts.

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:34.010
You're all beasts, so become beasts!

00:07:34.290 --> 00:07:35.750
What is he saying?

00:07:35.870 --> 00:07:37.010
Hiroyuki.

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:41.660
Lock one.

00:07:44.910 --> 00:07:46.410
Lock two.

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:49.110
Emi.

00:07:49.370 --> 00:07:52.360
Darn. Everyone, run!
 I'm out.

00:08:03.710 --> 00:08:05.840
Senpai, if you do that...

00:08:06.700 --> 00:08:08.540
It's the Establishment!

00:08:08.660 --> 00:08:09.580
Run!

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:11.580
It's coming here too.

00:08:13.330 --> 00:08:14.590
Well done.

00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:18.250
Now he's an enemy of
 the youth and society.

00:08:18.330 --> 00:08:20.730
And our beast will destroy him.

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:23.450
So you'll join our protest today?

00:08:23.540 --> 00:08:27.410
Yeah. It's a bit early,
 but let's begin.

00:08:32.110 --> 00:08:33.290
It's dead.

00:08:33.370 --> 00:08:35.120
The US Army's beast.

00:08:35.750 --> 00:08:37.990
So there's a way to revive it?

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:42.000
GaGon's cells have
 amazing regenerative power.

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:46.540
Add to that this drug,
 and it will instantly get huge.

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:48.910
I've tested it many times.

00:08:50.450 --> 00:08:52.870
It's a special cell activator.

00:08:53.620 --> 00:08:56.580
It can activate the cells of a beast.

00:08:56.790 --> 00:09:01.120
You can make an even bigger lizard
 from a lizard tail you cut off.

00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:03.330
This big?!

00:09:03.450 --> 00:09:04.910
Just as imagined.

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:07.950
GaGon's cells have high
 regenerative power.

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:09.820
What will you do with it?

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:14.450
First, we'll make money. And then...

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:19.910
We'll shock those
 talking about the Shinka Genroku era.

00:09:25.370 --> 00:09:27.660
Next, GaGon's cells...

00:09:29.910 --> 00:09:30.950
GaGon!

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:45.080
Government oppression!

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:46.700
Continue the peace march.

00:09:46.790 --> 00:09:49.870
Stop the time.
 I'll get Jiro during that.

00:09:54.910 --> 00:09:57.410
The Beastly Radio Wave guys were here.

00:09:57.540 --> 00:09:59.820
They joined it with the US Army beast.

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:05.080
Don't be afraid. This is a weapon the
 US Army was trying to put in Okinawa.

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:09.040
No, he's a soldier.
 He didn't want to go to war.

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:10.960
So he ran from the carrier.

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:13.700
An honest, military-refusing beast.

00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:19.200
We want to save him from the Japanese
 government and US Imperialism.

00:10:19.250 --> 00:10:21.850
We'll protest so he can live in peace.

00:10:22.040 --> 00:10:25.220
That's the true purpose
 of today's peace march.

00:10:25.700 --> 00:10:27.830
Guys, protect MegaGon.

00:10:33.410 --> 00:10:35.790
It's over if he kills students.

00:10:35.870 --> 00:10:37.900
Fuurouta, make him abandon Equus.

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:39.290
Got it.

00:10:51.870 --> 00:10:52.870
Meteortail!

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:06.220
MegaGon is us.
 Our anger is a beast.

00:11:07.330 --> 00:11:08.250
We are...

00:11:09.450 --> 00:11:10.480
beasts...

00:11:11.370 --> 00:11:14.120
Let's begin the peace march.

00:11:17.290 --> 00:11:21.450
It was said to be a protest
 by Japan Peace University students.

00:11:21.500 --> 00:11:25.950
But now many citizens have joined,
 and there are over 1,000 people.

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:30.250
Is there any danger,
 like him suddenly getting violent?

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:34.500
No. With MegaGon here,
 Tokyo will become peaceful.

00:11:34.700 --> 00:11:37.290
Even if bad guys come,
 he'll beat them.

00:11:37.330 --> 00:11:42.260
Everyone knows that MegaGon is
 a victim of society like us.

00:11:44.700 --> 00:11:46.700
Your beast is amazing.

00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:49.080
No, that's my little brother.

00:11:50.580 --> 00:11:53.290
I wonder where my brother is going.

00:11:55.700 --> 00:11:58.030
A kid obtained a beast.

00:11:58.580 --> 00:12:01.540
We've already defeated
 too many beasts.

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:05.030
If we attack, the students
 will be our enemies too.

00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:08.120
But making Jiro go violent...

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:10.410
It's a challenge to the Bureau.

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:12.250
There is a way.

00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:15.670
How about an accident?

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:20.370
Past 1:40 a.m. tonight,
 by the Shinjuku west exit overpass,

00:12:20.410 --> 00:12:24.580
a freight car and a tanker with
 the US Army's jet fuel will pass.

00:12:24.620 --> 00:12:28.410
If they crash due to small mistakes,
 it'll cause a huge fire.

00:12:29.450 --> 00:12:32.910
It's more than enough
 to burn a beast of that size.

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:36.190
It's at night,
 so there will be minimal casualties.

00:12:36.450 --> 00:12:40.940
The papers will say, "An accident
 from the driver missing the light."

00:12:41.330 --> 00:12:45.000
I heard you're
 a genius physicist, Yoshimura,

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:47.870
but it's like you can see the future.

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:51.620
Everything can be calculated.

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:54.620
Miss Emi.

00:12:58.660 --> 00:13:00.830
I asked you to throw that out.

00:13:07.370 --> 00:13:10.040
Ukyo Yamato of Beastly Radio Wave...

00:13:10.370 --> 00:13:11.890
It was you.

00:13:14.200 --> 00:13:16.450
It's called Appearance Reflection.

00:13:16.580 --> 00:13:19.270
Monsters need a model to transform.

00:13:19.870 --> 00:13:21.830
This face too, in the past...

00:13:21.870 --> 00:13:25.410
Beasts go wild,
 and you make superhumans kill them.

00:13:25.580 --> 00:13:29.370
To make society think
 superhumans are justice...

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:32.000
The Chief knows too, you know.

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:34.870
But Senpai...

00:13:35.450 --> 00:13:36.920
No way we'll tell him.

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:41.800
He truly loves superhumans.
 He wouldn't forgive this.

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:45.170
Then why have him continue this job?

00:13:45.870 --> 00:13:48.660
Senpai is hurt
 since he's a normal human.

00:13:48.870 --> 00:13:50.180
You really think so?

00:13:51.370 --> 00:13:52.890
You saw Jiro.

00:13:57.160 --> 00:13:59.080
Jiro is no normal human.

00:13:59.620 --> 00:14:03.410
He's much stronger
 and more dangerous than you think.

00:14:03.580 --> 00:14:06.660
So that's why I love Jiro.

00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:10.700
The one who
 has the right to love him...

00:14:11.620 --> 00:14:15.370
Is one who can stop him
 despite becoming like this.

00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:20.950
Simply put,
 there's a beast inside Jiro too.

00:14:21.500 --> 00:14:23.750
Inside any human, if you ask me.

00:14:24.120 --> 00:14:26.010
You're different?

00:14:26.450 --> 00:14:28.370
I'm a monster.

00:14:42.620 --> 00:14:46.110
No, Senpai.
 Miss Emi said you have to stay still.

00:14:47.040 --> 00:14:48.410
Where's Emi?

00:14:48.540 --> 00:14:52.000
She went to the mission
 to defeat the beast.

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:58.870
You heard why I hate beasts, right?

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:04.500
8 years ago,
 the beast Giganto Gon attacked Tokyo.

00:15:06.540 --> 00:15:09.500
(January, the 34th of Shinka Era
 Tokyo)

00:15:12.410 --> 00:15:15.700
It being my first
 close encounter with a beast,

00:15:15.750 --> 00:15:17.250
I got worked up.

00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:21.500
I don't know
 my real name or my parents.

00:15:22.040 --> 00:15:25.250
I was trapped in the lab
 since I was little.

00:15:26.200 --> 00:15:29.290
I felt like
 the beast let me go outside.

00:15:29.540 --> 00:15:31.950
Go wild! More!

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:35.580
The beast was killed
 by Rainbow Knight.

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:41.790
I knew that
 there was a beast inside me.

00:15:42.580 --> 00:15:46.000
Its desire is the destruction
 of this world.

00:15:46.870 --> 00:15:49.370
And I hate beasts when I'm like that.

00:15:50.120 --> 00:15:52.540
But the beast I truly hate is...

00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:55.430
somewhere I can't destroy it.

00:16:07.330 --> 00:16:08.450
Kikko.

00:16:11.410 --> 00:16:12.750
What are you doing?

00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:16.250
That's not it. I mean...

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:18.790
There's a beast inside me too.

00:16:19.450 --> 00:16:21.040
No there isn't.

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:25.540
I'm just making it
 look like there isn't.

00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:27.540
I'm fighting it a lot.

00:16:36.950 --> 00:16:39.580
Showing that would've been quick.

00:16:39.750 --> 00:16:42.330
That'd make me worse than a beast.

00:16:56.200 --> 00:16:58.620
Can it really easily go under?

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:03.700
It's evaded almost everything
 besides what wasn't removed in time.

00:17:03.830 --> 00:17:05.870
It's proof that MegaGon is safe.

00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:08.790
I'd like to see it
 destroy too, though.

00:17:09.290 --> 00:17:12.080
MegaGon will become
 an idol loved by all.

00:17:12.660 --> 00:17:15.800
He'll fight bad guys, so bring one.

00:17:16.370 --> 00:17:21.410
I guess he's more reliable than
 those weird superhuman things.

00:17:27.700 --> 00:17:31.620
Like wild animals,
 it seems to hate bright lights.

00:17:35.530 --> 00:17:37.540
(August 8th, the 42nd of Shinka Era,
 1:30 a.m.)

00:17:48.200 --> 00:17:49.660
What is it, GaGon?

00:17:53.700 --> 00:17:54.800
What's he doing?

00:18:04.500 --> 00:18:05.870
What was that?

00:18:06.040 --> 00:18:07.390
Fuurouta the Ghost.

00:18:07.910 --> 00:18:09.790
A friend of children.

00:18:11.410 --> 00:18:14.410
You guys must be sleepy,
 but please wake up.

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:20.410
The Princess is calling.

00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:33.050
Birds at this hour?

00:18:33.330 --> 00:18:34.290
Hang in there!

00:18:34.330 --> 00:18:35.580
Kill it, MegaGon.

00:18:35.660 --> 00:18:37.050
Strike them down.

00:18:42.080 --> 00:18:43.310
3 more minutes.

00:18:44.580 --> 00:18:45.680
It won't make it?

00:18:46.450 --> 00:18:47.700
Where's the tanker?

00:18:47.870 --> 00:18:50.120
Here. It'll depart soon.

00:18:50.290 --> 00:18:52.450
If we can stop him a bit longer...

00:18:52.580 --> 00:18:54.830
We can't use Jiro. What now?

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:02.870
Meteortail!

00:19:09.410 --> 00:19:10.830
Is this magic?

00:19:11.660 --> 00:19:13.340
Go, Miss Kikko!

00:19:25.040 --> 00:19:26.830
No more...

00:19:37.830 --> 00:19:40.040
The US Army's fuel transport.

00:19:40.660 --> 00:19:42.700
That's going to war too.

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:46.580
I made the traffic light green.

00:19:46.790 --> 00:19:47.950
It's here.

00:19:58.370 --> 00:19:59.420
Yes!

00:20:02.620 --> 00:20:03.680
What now?

00:20:08.080 --> 00:20:09.660
It didn't reach.

00:20:12.950 --> 00:20:16.000
Haven't done something
 not human in a while.

00:20:21.950 --> 00:20:24.410
Chugga, chugga.

00:20:25.290 --> 00:20:27.540
- Watch out. Run!
 - It's falling.

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:29.410
GaGon!

00:20:49.410 --> 00:20:50.750
GaGon.

00:21:01.540 --> 00:21:02.950
What are you doing?

00:21:10.200 --> 00:21:11.500
Amazing.

00:21:12.080 --> 00:21:13.790
- Wow.
 - It's a beast.

00:21:13.870 --> 00:21:16.660
- Go wild.
 - So cool!

00:21:18.080 --> 00:21:20.830
Come on. He's your ally.

00:21:21.120 --> 00:21:22.750
Why make it go wild?

00:21:22.830 --> 00:21:23.970
I know now.

00:21:24.620 --> 00:21:26.330
I like beasts.

00:21:26.500 --> 00:21:29.290
I know, so I'll make it popular...

00:21:29.410 --> 00:21:31.200
It's not about reason.

00:21:31.290 --> 00:21:35.830
I like them because
 humans can't understand them.

00:21:38.160 --> 00:21:40.230
MegaGon!

00:21:46.500 --> 00:21:50.660
Oh no. We'll have to get help
 from a superhuman now.

00:22:05.200 --> 00:22:10.390
Are you a messenger of nature?
 An ancient god? A victim of humanity?

00:22:11.080 --> 00:22:13.870
Or something we desired ourselves?

00:22:20.910 --> 00:22:22.770
- Kikko!
 - Don't call me that.

00:22:23.330 --> 00:22:25.080
Meteortail!

00:22:35.700 --> 00:22:38.500
No matter what you are, I'll fight.

00:22:39.120 --> 00:22:42.250
As long as there are kids
 who cry from your fire.

00:23:03.330 --> 00:23:05.290
MegaGon!

00:23:14.160 --> 00:23:17.000
I will fight.
 I will continue to fight.

00:23:17.750 --> 00:23:20.500
I'll fight beasts. That's my decision.

00:24:58.080 --> 00:25:00.080
We collected everything.

00:25:00.250 --> 00:25:03.120
It's nice we could experiment
 after a long time.

00:25:03.160 --> 00:25:05.040
Let's handle it with care.

00:25:10.790 --> 00:25:14.360
(Blood Product - Jiro Hitoyoshi)

00:25:14.360 --> 00:25:18.620
The beast craze ended in
 about a year and a half.

00:25:18.910 --> 00:25:23.830
The monster craze that came after...
 That's another story.

00:25:26.580 --> 00:25:29.790
Everyone,
 it's time for the Mountain Horses.

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:32.660
Hal, Freeze, Dee,
 and I'm Don the leader.

00:25:32.700 --> 00:25:36.080
If we're all here, it's nice and fun
 so let's laugh.

00:25:36.090 --> 00:25:40.450
No one's died from over-laughing.
 Excuse me for a bit.
